\caption(The two uses may reinforce or cancel. Dropping either path changes the objective derivative.)
\alttext(Six shared-weight coordinates show encoder, decoder and summed derivatives from the actual toy calculation.)

For an untied decoder D the derivatives are X transpose A for W and H transpose E for D.
Even starting at D=W transpose, separate Adam updates generally break that equality.
Adam of the shared gradient sum is not the sum of two independent Adam updates: each first
and second moment is computed from the combined derivative, including its squared cross term.

> Full geometry and independent parameter count

The tied census is dk+k+d=25,904; untied adds dk=25,088, giving 50,992. Biases are not tied.
The following graph traces the real code and decoder branches, counting each shared leaf once.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tied_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1853);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& x) {
        auto out = n::models::TiedAutoencoder(p, x);
        n::model_stage("ReLU encoder / shared W", x, out.code);
        n::model_stage("Sigmoid decoder / live W transpose", out.code, out.reconstruction);
        return out.reconstruction;
      },
      "Tied ReLU/sigmoid autoencoder: 784–32–784");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons           = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 25904 || p.size() != 3 || figure.parameter_count() != 25904 ||
      p.contains("decoder/W"))
    return 1;
  figure.save_svg("build/tied_architecture.svg");
  std::print("| parameter | scalars |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", name, p.at(name).numel());
}
